  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until the eighth broke it open.",
    "what_this_means": "Schlittler's 10 strikeouts over seven innings put them in position, and the bullpen held what mattered. But this game lived in the eighth inning. When Ben Rice's walk sparked three runs that the offense had been unable to find all night. They managed eight hits total, converted just one RISP situation into runs, and yet that one sequence late was enough. This is not a formula that scales across a season. One walk igniting a three-run rally in a game where they struggled to string together anything resembles desperation disguised as control. The margin between holding on and collapsing narrowed to a single inning.",
